            "bodyHtml": "<p>Complete the notes below. Write <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> for each answer.</p><div><div><strong>Rural Development — The Berbers</strong></div><p>The Berbers</p><ul><li>lived in various countries in North Africa</li><li>were driven from their homes during the 12th century</li><li>began to lead a nomadic life, moving across {{31}} and mountains</li></ul><p>Different Berber Lifestyles</p><ul><li>some Berbers, known as {{32}} nomads, moved twice a year</li><li>some Berbers were completely nomadic</li><li>some Berbers settled by oases, producing fruit, vegetables, and {{33}} to cook with</li><li>people and belongings were carried by {{34}}</li><li>settled Berbers lived in houses</li><li>nomadic Berbers used tents</li><li>settled communities organised themselves by holding regular meetings in the {{35}} of the village</li></ul><p>The Tuaregs</p><ul><li>if goatskins were unavailable, tents were made from {{36}} or palm-leaf mats</li><li>Tuareg labourers were the descendants of {{37}}</li><li>adult men always wore a {{38}} veil</li><li>some Tuaregs moved to Burkina Faso with their {{39}}</li></ul><p>Tuaregs and Timbuktu</p><ul><li>Timbuktu was settled by Tuaregs around 1000 years ago</li><li>the city built wealth on the salt and gold trades</li><li>some Tuaregs now work as {{40}} for the Malian Department of Tourism</li></ul></div>",
